<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb unemployment rate unchanged at 3.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb unemployment rate unchanged at 3.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's seasonally adjusted unemployment rate in February remained unchanged from January at 3.3 percent, while the jobs-to-applicants ratio fell to 0.73 from 0.76 a month earlier, the government said on Friday.</p>
<p>It was the first time since July 1995 that the jobs-to-applicants ratio had fallen from the previous month, the Labour Ministry said.</p>
<p>This means there were 73 job openings for every 100 job seekers.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the jobs data:</p>
<p> (Adjusted)			  February  January   Year ago</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		  3.3 pct   3.3 pct   3.3 pct</p>
<p>					 February  January   Year ago</p>
<p> Jobs-to-applicants ratio	 0.73	0.76	0.66</p>
<p> (Unadjusted)			February  January   Year ago</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		  3.5 pct   3.3 pct   3.4 pct</p>
<p> Number of unemployed	     2.30 million  2.22 million  2.24 million</p>
<p> Number of employed		February	year/year change</p>
<p> Overall				64.18 million	+1.9 pct</p>
<p>Main Industries:</p>
<p> Manufacturing			14.56 million	+2.3 pct</p>
<p> Services			     16.10 million	+3.1 pct</p>
<p> Wholesale, retail, restaurants 14.37 million	+0.4 pct</p>
<p> Construction			  6.82 million	+3.6 pct</p>
<p> Agriculture			   2.43 million	-4.0 pct</p>
